# Where the `@skema` scope comes from.
#
# The packages are spread across the group's projects — `@skema/model` is built
# and published by skema-language/skema, `@skema/diagram` by this repository —
# and a project-level registry endpoint only ever serves its own project. The
# *group* endpoint resolves across every project in skema-language, so this one
# line covers the whole scope regardless of which repo a package came from.
#
# 141817046 is the skema-language group. It is public, so installing needs no
# token at all; CI adds one anyway (see .gitlab-ci.yml) so this keeps working
# if a project is ever made private.
#
# This line also decides where `npm publish` uploads, which is the reverse of
# what one would expect: for a scoped package npm reads `@scope:registry` first
# and only falls back to `publishConfig.registry`. The group endpoint is
# read-only, so the publish job has to override this key on its command line —
# nothing written to $HOME can do it, a project .npmrc outranks that.
@skema:registry=https://gitlab.com/api/v4/groups/141817046/-/packages/npm/
